The standard enthalpy change (ΔH°rx) for a reaction can be calculated using the following equation:

ΔH°rx = Σ nΔH°f (products) - Σ nΔH°f (reactants)

where:

*   ΔH°rx is the standard enthalpy change of the reaction
*   n is the stoichiometric coefficient of each reactant and product in the balanced equation
*   ΔH°f is the standard enthalpy of formation of each reactant and product

