ΔT<sub>b = K<sub>b * m/M
where:
* ΔT<sub>b is the solution (in °C)
* K<sub>b is the solution constant of the solvent (in °C kg/ mol)
   for carbon tetr chloride, K_b = 5.03°C kg/mol
   
    m is the solution (in kg/ kg of solution)
    M is the solution of the solution (in g/mol)

