The sum of the terms $x^{2k}$ is a standard G.P. with $a = x^2$, $r = x^2$, and $n$ terms.
$$ \sum_{k=1}^n x^{2k} = \frac{x^2(x^{2n} - 1)}{x^2 - 1} = \frac{x^2(x^{2n} - 1)}{x^2 - 1} = \frac{x^{2n+2} - x^2}{x^2 - 1}. $$
The sum of the terms $x^k$ is a standard G.P. with $a = x$, $r = x$, and $n$ terms.
$$ \sum_{k=1}^n x^k = \frac{x(x^n - 1)}{x - 1} = \frac{x^{n+1} - x}{x - 1}. $$
The sum of the constant terms is
$$ \sum_{K = 1}^n 1 = n. $$
Therefore,
$$ S_n = \frac{x^{2n + 2} - x^2}{x^2 - 1} + 2 \frac{x^{n+1} - x}{x - 1} + n. $$
