We know that 1 kg of water vapor at 220°C needs 1858.5 kJ of energy to vapor.  We can use this to calculate the mass of the gas needed:

1858.5 kJ = m_g * 1.005 kJ/kg°C * 550°C

m_g = 1858.5 kJ / (1.1005 * 550) kg
m_g ≈ 3.14 kg

